---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

// Written 2026-07-28 from what the site actually does: free informational
// content, free tools (checklist, Emergency Card, rescue flow), optional
// registration via Brevo, GA4 behind consent, affiliate links possible
// outside the rescue flow. Keep it short, accurate, expandable.
const UPDATED = '28 July 2026';
---
<Base
  title="Terms of Use | Save My Gig"
  description="The rules for using Save My Gig: a free resource for working DJs, provided as is, with plain conditions and no surprises."
  path="/legal/terms"
  noindex
>
  <main class="wrap">
    <div class="status-line">LEGAL</div>
    <h1 style="margin-bottom:0.6rem">Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:2rem">Last updated: {UPDATED} · Part of <a href="/legal">the legal shelf</a></p>

    <h2 class="trm-sec">The agreement</h2>
    <p>
      Save My Gig (savemygig.com) is operated from Brazil by its founders. By
      using the site you agree to these terms. If you do not agree with them,
      do not use the site.
    </p>

    <h2 class="trm-sec">What the service is</h2>
    <p>
      Save My Gig is a free resource for working DJs: guides, reference pages,
      an emergency rescue flow, a pre-gig checklist and related tools. All of it
      is general information, not professional advice for your specific
      situation. The <a href="/legal/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a> covers what that
      means in practice, including the risk of data loss, and forms part of
      these terms.
    </p>

    <h2 class="trm-sec">Registration</h2>
    <p>
      Some free features ask you to register with an email address. You agree to
      provide a real address that is yours. Registration is free, requires no
      password, and every email we send has a one-click unsubscribe. How we
      handle your data is described in the
      <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. We may withdraw registered
      features from an address that abuses them.
    </p>

    <h2 class="trm-sec">Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      Use the site as a DJ, not as a target. You agree not to disrupt or
      overload the service, not to attempt to gain access to systems or data
      that are not yours, not to scrape or bulk-copy the content for
      republication, and not to use the forms to send spam or content that is
      unlawful.
    </p>

    <h2 class="trm-sec">Our content</h2>
    <p>
      The content of this site (text, structure, checklists, design) is
      © 2026 Save My Gig™ unless stated otherwise. You are welcome to use it
      personally, print it, and share links to it. Republishing it wholesale, or
      presenting it as your own, is not permitted without written permission.
      Third-party names and trademarks (AlphaTheta, Pioneer DJ, rekordbox and
      others) belong to their respective owners; we are not affiliated with
      them.
    </p>

    <h2 class="trm-sec">Links and affiliate links</h2>
    <p>
      The site links to third-party sites and products we do not control and are
      not responsible for. Some product links may be affiliate links, meaning we
      may earn a commission at no additional cost to you. This never changes
      what we recommend, and there are no affiliate or sponsored links inside
      the emergency rescue flow.
    </p>

    <h2 class="trm-sec">No warranty, limited liability</h2>
    <p>
      The service is provided free of charge and <strong>"as is"</strong>,
      without warranty of any kind. To the fullest extent permitted by law, our
      liability for any loss arising from your use of the site is excluded. The
      full text of this exclusion is in the
      <a href="/legal/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a>. Nothing in these terms limits
      liability where it would be unlawful to do so.
    </p>

    <h2 class="trm-sec">Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update the site, the tools and these terms at any time. The date at
      the top of this page tells you when the terms last changed. Continuing to
      use the site after a change means you accept the updated terms.
    </p>

    <h2 class="trm-sec">Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of Brazil. If a court finds part of
      these terms unenforceable, the rest remains in force.
    </p>

    <h2 class="trm-sec">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms:
      <a href="mailto:info@savemygig.com">info@savemygig.com</a>, or use the
      <a href="/feedback">feedback form</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .trm-sec { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 2rem 0 0.7rem; text-transform: none; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  main p { color: var(--text-dim); }
  main p strong { color: var(--text); }
</style>
